 591: #  ---- D11 (round 5): the CLASS CLOSURE for the stored-bit filtering class -------------------
 592: #  WHY A CLASS CLOSURE RATHER THAN TWO MORE ROWS.  Table 4 came back clean and the ask-again then
 593: #  found filtering escapes at MASK0 and BASE1 -- the SECOND consecutive pass to find one breach of
 594: #  one class, which is the carrier's trigger to stop buying cells one at a time and enumerate the
 595: #  whole space in ONE diff.  The space is {MASK, BASE} x {window 0, window 1} x {reserved-bit
 596: #  filtering, field-source selection, zero acceptance, invalid-field rejection}, and the cells that
 597: #  no existing row held are R1-R6 below.  *** THAT SPACE IS FOUR ARMS OF SIX: CONF and TB_ENA filter
 598: #  a stored field too and were left out -- closed by D12, which is where the correction lives. ***
 599: #
 600: #  THE INPUTS ARE THE 64-BIT COMPLEMENTS OF THE STORE MASKS, and that is the whole trick:
 601: #      ~0xfff00000  == 0xffffffff000fffff   (MASK: architected bits 20-31)
 602: #      ~0x3fff00000 == 0xfffffffc000fffff   (BASE: W_BASE 20-31, SG 32, WEN 33)
 603: #  so EVERY reserved bit is set and EVERY architected bit is clear.  A store mask widened by even
 604: #  one bit therefore reads back that bit instead of zero, and a mask NARROWED by one bit is caught
 605: #  at the SEED readback, whose value sets every architected bit.  One pair of writes per register
 606: #  covers narrowing and widening in both directions.
 607: #
 608: #  AND THE FIELD-SOURCE CELL FALLS OUT OF THE SAME INPUT.  With the shipped normalisation
 609: #  f = (idata & 0xfff00000) >> 20 the complement gives f = 0, f & (f+1) = 0, LEGAL, stored as 0.
 610: #  Validate the RAW input instead and f = 0xffffffff000, f & (f+1) = 0xffffffff000 != 0, DECLINED --
 611: #  so the seed value is retained and the row reds.  Reserved input bits 32-63 become deciding field
 612: #  bits 12-43 under raw validation, which is why the complement separates the two readings and a
 613: #  merely-large legal value would not.
 614: #
 615: #  Each row scores the PAIR (seed readback, final readback): the seed is not a free-standing row
 616: #  because a rule that rejects the seed and a rule that rejects the final write are different
 617: #  mutants, and one row that names both states separates them without inflating the denominator.
 618: S_MASK = 0xffffffff000fffff        # ~0xfff00000
 619: S_BASE = 0xfffffffc000fffff        # ~0x3fff00000
